# Release Engineering Workflow

Full policy: `docs/RELEASE_ENGINEERING_WORKFLOW.md`  
Hardening notes: `docs/releases/RELEASE-ENGINEERING-HARDENING.md`

## Source of truth

`main` and `origin/main` only. Feature branches are temporary.

## Canonical deploy entry

```bash
# When origin/main has migrations not yet in /opt (schema-first):
bash deploy/manage_deploy.sh migrate release
sudo bash deploy/manage_deploy.sh deploy full
bash deploy/manage_deploy.sh verify-release
```

Never deploy feature branches, dirty trees, or local-only commits.
Do not skip `migrate release` when `/opt` lacks required migration files.
`deploy full` still runs post-sync Alembic (idempotent no-op after successful schema-first).

## Lifecycle

Architecture Review → Implementation → Tests → Review → Fixes → Acceptance → Merge `main` → Validate → Push `origin/main` → (schema-first `migrate release` when required) → Deploy → Verify

## Hard rules

- Never merge or `git push origin main` without explicit user approval (ask separately).
- Never use `ALLOW_DIRTY_SYNC` / `DEPLOY_LOCAL_MAIN` / `--no-backup-db` for normal release deploys.
- Identity chain must match: origin/main == build-info == frontend identity == /api/build == APP_RELEASE.
- Release deploy stages: backup → build → deploy (incl. post-sync migrate) → verify → restart → smoke.
- Schema-first cutover: status → backup db → migrate release → verify schema head → deploy full → health → build-info → smoke → verify-release.
- New deploy/release features go into `manage_deploy.sh` only (no new standalone deploy scripts except bootstrap/recovery).
